# Plan Template And Close Enforcement

**Activation:** `alwaysApply: false` — when triggers in `agent-discipline-core.mdc` match, **Read this file before editing**. Triggered rules are mandatory, not optional.

Agents must not treat plan structure or the **close sequence** as optional under time pressure—**including bugfixes and hotfixes with no plan file**. This rule is the **short enforcement reminder**; detail lives in **`plan-creation-contract.mdc`**, **`plan-live-disk-sync.mdc`**, **`plan-completion-gate.mdc`**, **`implementation-review-workflow.mdc`**, and **`docs/plans/PLAN_TEMPLATE.md`**.

## Plan disk sync (chat does not count)

Per **`plan-live-disk-sync.mdc`**:

1. **First plan turn** — **Write** the full plan to **`<workspace_root>/.cursor/plans/<name>.plan.md`** (not chat-only, not CreatePlan-only, **not Plan UI / edit window before disk exists**).
2. **Every later turn** — **Write/StrReplace** that file **before** reporting progress, operator results, or completed todos.
3. **Operator discovery** — pending commands grouped by Compose service; completed commands become **Completed findings** rows (asked vs found) and are **removed** from Pending.
4. **Plan UI / TodoWrite** — secondary mirrors only; **do not open or edit Plan UI until the disk file exists** (`plan-live-disk-sync.mdc`); frontmatter todo `status` on disk is what the Plan UI should reflect.

## Every implementation plan must include

1. All required sections in order per **`plan-creation-contract.mdc`** (Plan disk file → Problem and facts → Operator discovery when needed → Approach → Testing → Implementation → Cursor rules → Final code review).
2. **`Final code review (mandatory before implementation close)`** per **`PLAN_TEMPLATE.md`**.
3. **`Post-implementation review (required before close)`** per **`PLAN_TEMPLATE.md`**.
4. Final YAML todo:

```yaml
- id: post-implementation-review
  content: "Final senior code review (diff + workflow) clean; structured self-review in chat (why it works, edge cases, convention check)"
  status: pending
```

Copy the full frontmatter/todo block from **`docs/plans/PLAN_TEMPLATE.md`** when authoring new plans.

## When the user asks for a plan

Unless they explicitly request a **narrow exception** (answer-only, trivial typo/comment with no behavior change):

1. **Read** **`docs/plans/PLAN_TEMPLATE.md`** and **`plan-live-disk-sync.mdc`** before authoring.
2. **Write** the plan to **`.cursor/plans/<name>.plan.md`** in the same turn (CreatePlan or chat alone does not satisfy this). **Do not** open the Cursor Plan UI / edit window for a plan that is not already on disk at that path.
3. **Match** PLAN_TEMPLATE structure on disk.
4. **End** with **`post-implementation-review`** as the **last** todo.

**Treat as full-plan requests** (use PLAN_TEMPLATE + final review sections):

- “Create a plan per PLAN_TEMPLATE.md”
- “Include final code review per plan-creation-contract”
- “Implement this plan” / attached plan file / Cursor Plan todos
- “Plan mode” output for non-trivial implementation work

## When implementing or closing (all code changes)

Per **`plan-completion-gate.mdc`** → *Blocking close gate*, every **non-trivial code change** must end with three required chat sections (**Agent rule dispatch**, **Final code review (senior engineer pass)**, **Post-implementation review**) in the **same final turn**—not only plan-driven work.

**During plan implementation:** per **`plan-completion-gate.mdc`** → *Plan YAML todo sync*, update each finished plan todo to `status: completed` in the plan frontmatter (status-only edits allowed even when plan prose must not change). Use the **same todo ids** as the plan YAML in `TodoWrite`.

**Close sequence order:**

1. **Agent rule dispatch** — list triggered **`*.mdc`** rules Read (or **N/A** with reason); see **`agent-discipline-core.mdc`** task router.
2. **Final code review (senior engineer pass)** — review the full diff and every workflow the change touches; when `cursor-rules/*.mdc` changed, confirm dual registration in `agent-discipline-core.mdc` and `hook_task_router.py`; fix anything a senior reviewer would block on merge; re-run relevant tests.
3. **Structured chat self-review** — after step 2 is clean, write **Why it works**, **Edge cases** (≥3 realistic failure modes), and **Convention check** (tests, triggered rules, layer wiring, **`test_runs/`** logging; confirm senior pass had no unfixed gaps).

**Do not mark the task, plan, or todos done** until all close steps are complete (and, when a plan is active, plan YAML todos are synced and **`post-implementation-review`** is complete). If step 3 surfaces a new gap, return to step 2 before close.

## Recommended Cursor User Rule (paste in Settings → Rules → User Rules)

Paste as the **first** user rule for highest signal:

> Follow `agent-discipline-core.mdc` pre-close checklist every code change. BLOCKING CLOSE GATE: before "done/fixed/complete", include (1) ## Agent rule dispatch — list Read triggered `hpcperfstats/cursor-rules/*.mdc` files or N/A, (2) ## Final code review (senior engineer pass), (3) ## Post-implementation review (Why it works, Edge cases ≥3, Convention check). Read triggered rules before editing matching paths. If I reply "Close gate incomplete" or "Rule not read: <name>", redo without argument.

## Overlap

- **`plan-live-disk-sync.mdc`** — disk authority, operator discovery lifecycle, every-turn updates.
- **`plan-creation-contract.mdc`** — mandatory plan authoring structure and completion bar.
- **`plan-completion-gate.mdc`** — execution gate: senior final code review then structured chat self-review before close.
- **`implementation-review-workflow.mdc`** — pre-code planning and post-code review content.
